# Grubstake's camp lots (WFC, a sprawl: the user, 2026-10-26, "WFC with larger chunks and very few walls so we get a
# sprawl that doesn't block movement"). Each lot: a header "tile <name> <weight>", then 12 rows of 12 characters.
#   ' ' bare ground   ':' gravel track (2 wide, through the middle of an edge or not at all)   '.' gravel yard
#   '%' hazard plate (under a pad or a machine's apron only)
#   'D' depot 4x4   'F' fabricator 3x3   'G' generator 2x2   'R' radar 3x3   'K' storage tank 3x3   'T' turret 2x2
#   'V' a parked vehicle 2x2   'W' a wreck (scrap) 2x2   'X' junk barricade 1x1   'C' crate 1x1   'P' wooden pole   'L' lamp
#   'O' an ore heap 2x2   'I' a pipe 1x1
#   '+' the rest of a building's footprint (its letter at the top-left)
# Two lots fit where their touching edges agree; a track may run off the camp's edge into the wild. Lots keep their
# buildings off their own edge, so every edge is bare ground or a track: the camp is open everywhere.

